    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] Based on the novel \"Beau Sabreur\" by P. C. Wren, who also wrote \"Beau Geste\", the film is about a desert-bound member of the French Foreign Legion who exposes a betrayer to the Legion and is then sent on a mission among the Arabs to conclude the signing of a crucial peace treaty.\n[2] Emanuel, who is ranked by some critics as one of the best and most neglected poets of the 20th century, published more than 300 poems, 13 individual books, an influential anthology of African American literature, an autobiography, and more.\n[3] He is remembered best for \"Beau Geste\", a much-filmed book of 1924, involving the French Foreign Legion in North Africa."
